<title>JAPAN: Japan 2-yr note auction lowest price 99.90.</title>
<headline>Japan 2-yr note auction lowest price 99.90.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>An auction of 120 billion yen in two-year government notes on Thursday produced the following results, the Ministry of Finance said:</p>
<p>Lowest price	  99.90    Stop rate	   0.750 pct</p>
<p>Average price	 99.93    Average yield     0.733 pct</p>
<p>Total bids	   289.7 billion yen</p>
<p>Accepted Bids	116.3 billion yen</p>
<p>Bids accepted at lowest price 99.4897 pct</p>
<p>Issue date    May 20, 1997   Maturity    May 20, 1999</p>
<p>Coupon payment     May 20, Nov 20</p>
</text>
